      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, I should\u0027ve mention that. It\u0027s the same reason why the \"ApexSignature\" has the \"size\" field. Microdroid signature itself is a protobuf, regular file, the size of which is not aligned to a certain boundary. But when it\u0027s mapped to a partition and accessed via a block device inside the guest VM, we can\u0027t query the size of, say, /dev/block/vdc1 with lseek(SEEK_END) or ioctl(BLOCKGETSIZE64). (These return some value which is not exactly the original size of the file). That\u0027s why we need a \"length\" to read the exact protobuf message from the path.\n\nOf course, there\u0027s many alternative ways. One might be to put a fixed-sized footer at the end of \"aligned boundary\" so that every signature guarantees to have no extra bytes at the end.",
